==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[taws]]

===Etymology===
Apparently a plural form of {{term|taw}}, though attested earlier.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tɔːz/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɔːz|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|chiefly|Scotland|lang=en}} A [[leather]] [[strap]] or thong which is split into (typically three) tails, used for [[corporal punishment]] in schools, applied to the palm of the hands or buttocks.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|taws}}

# {{cx|transitive|chiefly|Scotland|lang=en}} To beat with a tawse.

